			title: "Machines"
			x: 5.0d
			y: 10.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["77ECA9A3DDFB480D"]
			description: ["The &6Spintronic Cluster Tool&r lays magnetic layers a few atoms thick, with a magnesia barrier between them that nothing older can deposit. It also patterns racetrack nanowires and grows oxide films by pulsed laser. A UIV hull, about 1,350 gum metal and 870 mu-metal shield casings, the magnetron parts, and sputter targets from the melter. The shape is about 31 by 11 by 31 and about 2,350 blocks: GTM's Terminal places about 2,300 blocks per pass, so a structure this large takes two. The magnetic tunnel junction die, and through it the MRAM wafer, the racetrack chip and the multiferroic films of the MESO logic die. The Spintronic Cluster Tool also takes over the old racetrack fab and the oxide pulsed laser chamber: racetrack patterning and the oxide films run in it. Targets and silicon-28 by ME; the dies come out in a chest."]
			icon: "gtceu:mtj_sputter_cluster"
			id: "1595ABB6AB097B3E"
			rewards: [{ id: "1835656A2A02BB85", type: "xp", xp: 120 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "7F3A5AD491D6BAC7", item: "gtceu:mtj_sputter_cluster", type: "item" }
				{ id: "1875D9D0EB3D2220", item: "grindless:gum_metal_casing", type: "item" }
				{ id: "716CAADB05679496", item: "grindless:mu_metal_shield_casing", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Spintronic Cluster Tool"
			x: 10.0d
			y: 10.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["77ECA9A3DDFB480D"]
			description: ["The &6YIG LPE Furnace&r dips a wafer into a molten bath and draws it out coated in a garnet film that carries spin waves almost without loss. A UIV hull, the robust casing, three heater bands and a platinum crucible. The magnonic bus the spintronic mainframe is wired with. Wafers and charge by ME; films take time, so run it in a stack of machines."]
			icon: "gtceu:yig_lpe_furnace"
			id: "7486DF37973BED77"
			rewards: [{ id: "5AEFFDB492571336", type: "xp", xp: 120 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "5A6D73BE11783F0A", item: "gtceu:yig_lpe_furnace", type: "item" }
				{ id: "1571A221A995FDFB", item: "gtceu:robust_machine_casing", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "YIG LPE Furnace"
			x: 10.0d
			y: 15.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7486DF37973BED77"]
			description: ["The &6Van der Waals Stacker&r from UEV also takes the UXV work: it peels flakes of tungsten ditelluride, Fe3GeTe2 and boron nitride and presses them into a heterostack, and its assembly mode builds the magnetoelectric and MESO layers of the spintronic wafer. The UEV stacker: about 290 silicon carbide composite and 280 photonic casings, with stable casings and trinium coils. The shape is about 1,000 blocks. Nothing new is built for UXV; the stacking mode is selected by recipe. The SOT heterostack, the ME-on-spin layer and the MESO die. Flakes by ME; the stack is delicate, so output into a dedicated chest."]
			icon: "gtceu:vdw_stacker"
			id: "7E9BF22B379A4CEB"
			rewards: [{ id: "3785B23E8D650F68", type: "xp", xp: 120 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [{ id: "70F5A440F4C275E2", item: "gtceu:vdw_stacker", type: "item" }]
			title: "Van der Waals Stacker"
			x: 12.5d
			y: 15.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["77ECA9A3DDFB480D"]
			description: ["The &6SHeQUID Works&r fills two baths of superfluid helium, joins them through an array and seals the pair as a weak link. A UIV hull, the cryostat casing and a supply of superfluid helium. The weak link cell and the gyro the UXV sensor is built from. Helium by pipe; keep the nanoaperture arrays stocked by ME."]
			icon: "gtceu:shequid_works"
			id: "7AE0BEC91F59A48B"
			rewards: [{ id: "52B703A60683FA50", type: "xp", xp: 120 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "17B5F50EB60BAFDD", item: "gtceu:shequid_works", type: "item" }
				{ id: "58870364B8D50034", item: "grindless:cryostat_casing", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "SHeQUID Works"
			x: 7.5d
			y: 14.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["77ECA9A3DDFB480D"]
			description: ["Collide uranium on curium and the two swap nucleons, leaving neutron-rich nuclei near the island of stability. The &6MNT Collider&r stops them in gas and weighs them by flight time. A UIV hull, about 2,000 gum metal and 800 pulsed field casings, a long beamline and a gas catcher. The shape is about 91 by 13 by 15 and about 3,550 blocks: GTM's Terminal places about 2,300 blocks per pass, so a structure this large takes two. Island nuclides, and with them the island chart the OpV research asks for. Targets and ion sources by ME; the yield is a trickle, so send it straight to the chart."]
			icon: "gtceu:mnt_collider"
			id: "112452274F3E9096"
			rewards: [{ id: "73062A763AF5AE20", type: "xp", xp: 120 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "328576CEF538773F", item: "gtceu:mnt_collider", type: "item" }
				{ id: "739D607C0B0D226D", item: "grindless:gum_metal_casing", type: "item" }
				{ id: "34088A941F775F3A", item: "grindless:pulsed_field_casing", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "MNT Collider"
			x: 10.0d
			y: 9.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["77ECA9A3DDFB480D"]
			description: ["The black hole already pulls its companion apart. The &6Stellar Elevator&r heats the star's surface where the pull is strongest and catches the stream as plasma. It works at Cygnus X-1 only. A UIV hull, about 740 pulsed field casings, silicon carbide composite for the shaft and a stack of coil rings, with power for the heating. The shape is about 23 by 57 by 23 and about 4,070 blocks: GTM's Terminal places about 2,300 blocks per pass, so a structure this large takes two. Stellar plasma, which the mass filter cuts and the condensation tower cools. The plasma goes by pipe to the filter; a tank in between keeps the lift steady."]
			icon: "gtceu:stellar_elevator"
			id: "1F198C897B7C73D8"
			rewards: [{ id: "132D17CCC398E465", type: "xp", xp: 150 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "30E9DF75D366723A", item: "gtceu:stellar_elevator", type: "item" }
				{ id: "780BD11D151D3619", item: "grindless:pulsed_field_casing", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Stellar Elevator"
			x: 12.5d
			y: 9.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1F198C897B7C73D8"]
			description: ["A spinning plasma flings its heavy ions outward. The &6Plasma Mass Filter&r cuts the star into hydrogen, helium, carbon-nitrogen-oxygen and heavy cuts, and cleans disk plasma the same way. A UIV hull, about 260 pulsed field casings, silicon carbide composite for the drum and the radial ports. The shape is about 37 by 15 by 15 and about 1,440 blocks. The cuts that feed the Mk6 ring and the condensation tower. One tank per cut, each on its own pipe; the filter does not forgive a mixed line."]
			icon: "gtceu:plasma_mass_filter"
			id: "344ECF8428D0E972"
			rewards: [{ id: "33A27B0F41FAB8AF", type: "xp", xp: 150 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "1D91DE28ABFA9088", item: "gtceu:plasma_mass_filter", type: "item" }
				{ id: "3464B7DE3E9551E5", item: "grindless:pulsed_field_casing", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Plasma Mass Filter"
			x: 17.5d
			y: 9.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["344ECF8428D0E972"]
			description: ["The gas falling into the hole spins in a disk hot enough to glow in X-rays. The &6Accretion Disk Skimmer&r skims its edge and sends the catch to the mass filter. A UIV hull, about 190 pulsed field casings, silicon carbide composite for the bowl and a rim of coils round it. The shape is about 19 by 9 by 19 and about 580 blocks. Filtered disk plasma, the fuel of the FRC former and the BZ dynamo. Route the catch by pipe to the filter and keep the surplus in a tank."]
			icon: "gtceu:accretion_disk_skimmer"
			id: "1887C02641FE7714"
			rewards: [{ id: "5F1B3C559EA8C45A", type: "xp", xp: 150 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
