				{ id: "17889A5DB785D254", item: "gtceu:bz_dynamo", type: "item" }
				{ id: "12F62BBA9D7270FC", item: "grindless:gum_metal_casing", type: "item" }
				{ id: "319F8F48AA17BB95", item: "grindless:pulsed_field_casing", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "BZ Dynamo"
			x: 25.0d
			y: 9.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["795E541822A26BC7", "344ECF8428D0E972"]
			description: ["The &6Mk6 Fusion Reactor&r burns as a star does: hot CNO, then helium, carbon and oxygen. A direct converter takes the power off each ash, and one burn's ash is quenched into the next one's fuel. A UXV hull, UXV components, about 250 UXV fusion casings, 2,000 gum metal and 1,300 pulsed field casings, the Mk5 coil and fusion glass. The shape is about 45 by 11 by 45 and about 4,100 blocks: GTM's Terminal places about 2,300 blocks per pass, so a structure this large takes two. The plasma and burn quests that follow. Fuel and coolant by pipe; a ring that runs a star's burning stages on demand is fiction, so plan the ash chain first."]
			icon: "gtceu:uxv_fusion_reactor"
			id: "5CE1C18D40A0B8E2"
			rewards: [{ id: "13D1BD31FCFD288E", type: "xp", xp: 250 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "5C330717261B2CB1", item: "gtceu:uxv_fusion_reactor", type: "item" }
				{ id: "504F99CB405FBA6C", item: "grindless:uxv_fusion_casing", type: "item" }
				{ id: "7E92A81B66B7CB58", item: "grindless:gum_metal_casing", type: "item" }
				{ id: "765DC107E4785A6F", item: "grindless:pulsed_field_casing", type: "item" }
				{ id: "1502DF9352D1546C", item: "gtceu:fusion_glass", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Mk6 Fusion Reactor"
			x: 27.5d
			y: 10.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["586BAF51DA2477E3"]
			description: ["Deep in a neutron star's crust the nuclei melt into rods, sheets and holes that physicists call pasta. A glitch shakes the crust loose, and the &6Pasta Extractor&r times it. A UIV hull, about 260 pasta containment and 80 pulsed field casings, and a receiver cage. The shape is about 21 by 11 by 11 and about 490 blocks. Raw pasta, the start of every pasta item. Neutronium pellets by ME; wait for a glitch and collect the haul."]
			icon: "gtceu:pasta_extractor"
			id: "1C34EDB89AD1F5C9"
			rewards: [{ id: "1121096DA82C1238", type: "xp", xp: 120 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "184DA14CA333EC3E", item: "gtceu:pasta_extractor", type: "item" }
				{ id: "5CD0B6F5A063C89A", item: "grindless:pulsed_field_casing", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Pasta Extractor"
			x: 20.0d
			y: 5.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1C34EDB89AD1F5C9"]
			description: ["The &6Pasta Mill&r separates the rods from the sheets inside a cage that keeps each one squeezed, pulls spaghetti phase through aerogel into strand wire, and presses lasagna phase onto a tungsten-fibre billet as plate. The anti-phase residue goes to the core sample the gate keeps. Pasta as wire or plate is fiction: outside a neutron star it would fly apart at once. A UIV hull, about 1,670 pasta containment and 810 pulsed field casings and the pasta hatches. The mill also takes over the old draw bench and laminator: the draw line and the press line are modes of this one machine. The shape is about 55 by 13 by 19 and about 2,850 blocks: GTM's Terminal places about 2,300 blocks per pass, so a structure this large takes two. Pasta strand wire, which the motor, the field generator and the SMES cell are wound with, and lasagna plate for the UXV hull. Raw pasta by ME; send each phase to its own line, and stock a few spools and plates."]
			icon: "gtceu:pasta_phase_sorter"
			id: "353D67B60E559EE1"
			rewards: [{ id: "75883048E114CE67", type: "xp", xp: 120 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "58C6F95474C92833", item: "gtceu:pasta_phase_sorter", type: "item" }
				{ id: "519A95E90CAF45FF", item: "grindless:gum_metal_casing", type: "item" }
				{ id: "1122F772807F4279", item: "grindless:pulsed_field_casing", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Pasta Mill"
			x: 22.5d
			y: 5.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["353D67B60E559EE1"]
			description: [
				"The &6Lasagna Plate&r is the structural plate of the UXV hull and of every UXV part: a tungsten-fibre billet with a lasagna phase pressed onto it."
				"The Pasta Mill makes it from the phase and a billet, which the sorting row supplies. It unlocks the UXV hull and, through it, every UXV machine. Plates stack quickly, so feed phase and billets by ME and send the plates on to the hull line."
			]
			icon: "grindless:lasagna_plate"
			id: "34D1D9ED3F6FBC67"
			rewards: [{ id: "16164FF0FF0A3286", type: "xp", xp: 80 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "503BA155D586710D", item: "grindless:lasagna_plate", type: "item" }]
			title: "Lasagna Plate"
			x: 27.5d
			y: 6.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["353D67B60E559EE1"]
			description: ["Above a pulsar's magnetic poles the field tears charges off the surface. The &6Polar Cap Tap&r lowers an electrode into that current and burns through it, at Vela only. A UIV hull, about 270 gum metal and 65 pulsed field casings, and a mast of insulator rings. The shape is about 13 by 17 by 13 and about 485 blocks. Power at Vela, for the gate hold and the machines out there. Electrodes by ME; the voltage is real, a way to collect it is not."]
			icon: "gtceu:polar_cap_tap"
			id: "50C6BE5A52F4F9A0"
			rewards: [{ id: "71D74C5B44B540E7", type: "xp", xp: 120 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "30987312A1343006", item: "gtceu:polar_cap_tap", type: "item" }
				{ id: "7A9AC387C2CC27DE", item: "grindless:gum_metal_casing", type: "item" }
				{ id: "745EB7346D03FE88", item: "grindless:pulsed_field_casing", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Polar Cap Tap"
			x: 27.5d
			y: 5.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5A539FCEC01451BA"]
			description: ["The star's core was thrown out in clumps still rich in what it made as it died. The &6Ejecta Knot Sweeper&r sweeps them up, behind a shield bow. A UIV hull, the Whipple shield casing and a filter collector. Ejecta knot dust, and titanium-44 from it. Shield weave by ME; the dust comes back by hopper."]
			icon: "gtceu:ejecta_knot_sweeper"
			id: "12376A5961A338E7"
			rewards: [{ id: "56D9BE7C40325044", type: "xp", xp: 120 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "32CE7A9CD71B6B2E", item: "gtceu:ejecta_knot_sweeper", type: "item" }
				{ id: "1CFA9454DF74F43F", item: "grindless:whipple_shield_casing", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Ejecta Knot Sweeper"
			x: 27.5d
			y: 3.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["12376A5961A338E7"]
			description: ["Slow a core's positrons into positronium, cool it, then let it annihilate all at once into a beam. The &6Annihilation Laser Works&r makes the gamma laser module. A UIV hull, the robust casing as a gamma shield and a Penning trap. The gamma laser module, and the UXV emitter built round it. Titanium-44 cores by ME; the modules are few, so keep them in a chest."]
			icon: "gtceu:annihilation_laser_works"
			id: "37FCF1CA912EC06F"
			rewards: [{ id: "3D80D2BB89E2FB14", type: "xp", xp: 120 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "371ACA9B6E1D5853", item: "gtceu:annihilation_laser_works", type: "item" }
				{ id: "3D5BB3952F16DA90", item: "gtceu:robust_machine_casing", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Annihilation Laser Works"
			x: 30.0d
			y: 7.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["37FCF1CA912EC06F"]
			description: ["A gamma-ray laser is fiction: nobody has built one. This one goes into the UXV emitter."]
			icon: "grindless:gamma_laser_module"
			id: "1E256F6A845C72DE"
			rewards: [{ id: "3AFF455A942A356F", type: "xp", xp: 80 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "5A8E57369AFB352C", item: "grindless:gamma_laser_module", type: "item" }]
			title: "Gamma Laser Module"
			x: 32.5d
			y: 7.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["103E024FEAF25DDC"]
			description: [
				"The spintronic wafer, X1 of the UXV Lines chart: a silicon-28 wafer carrying memory, racetrack, oscillators, spin-wave bus, magnetoelectric switch and spin-orbit readout."
				"Nine modules, one after another. The Spintronic Cluster Tool, the vdW stacker and the Photonic Foundry do most of the work."
			]
			icon: "grindless:spintronic_wafer"
			id: "3463B33FE3C32710"
			rewards: [ ]
			shape: "circle"
			size: 0.75d
			tasks: [{ id: "3D1457E10AF400E7", type: "checkmark" }]
			title: "UXV Spintronic Wafer"
			x: 27.0d
			y: 19.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3463B33FE3C32710"]
			description: ["Spins that last need a silicon with no nuclear spin of its own, so the line starts with silicon-28 and a CMOS wafer, the floor under every layer after it. The hot cell enriches silicon dust with hydrogen fluoride into silicon-28 dust (circuit 5). Zone refining melts it under argon into an ingot (circuit 6, 800 ticks); the cutter slices a wafer with water (400 ticks). The ion implanter loads hydrogen (circuit 6). The MOCVD reactor grows a hafnia gate and a titanium nitride gate (circuit 10, 700 ticks), and the Photonic Foundry lays tungsten vias and a copper layer (circuit 17). The 28Si M1 Wafer, which every later module is grown on. Silicon, acid and argon by ME and by pipe; wafers pass from machine to machine by pattern provider."]
			icon: "grindless:si28_cmos_wafer"
			id: "794B4368FD9DDBD0"
			rewards: [{ id: "77EA927AAB1E81EA", type: "xp", xp: 120 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "3FAC50AC9E54EDAE", item: "grindless:si28_fz_wafer", type: "item" }
				{ id: "161E319476CD2C17", item: "grindless:si28_cmos_wafer", type: "item" }
				{ id: "3484740DC0476851", item: "grindless:si28_m1_wafer", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Silicon-28 and the CMOS Wafer"
			x: 29.5d
			y: 19.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["794B4368FD9DDBD0"]
			description: ["The magnetic tunnel junctions that store a bit as the direction of a magnet. They are laid on the M1 wafer by the &6Spintronic Cluster Tool&r. The Cluster Tool sputters a heusler target, a magnesia barrier and a tantalum seed onto the wafer under argon (circuit 2, 800 ticks); the heusler powder comes back. The nitride magnet works anneals it (circuit 9), the ion implanter etches it (circuit 9), and the Photonic Foundry caps it with copper (circuit 18). The racetrack module, which writes tracks over the MRAM wafer. Targets by ME from the melter; return the heusler powder to the target line so nothing is lost."]
			icon: "grindless:mram_wafer"
			id: "37CEE1000998A174"
			rewards: [{ id: "17754FD16A58A576", type: "xp", xp: 140 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "160428A29CEC8607", item: "grindless:mram_stack_wafer", type: "item" }
				{ id: "1799A133D0E9E923", item: "grindless:mram_wafer", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "MRAM Stack"
			x: 33.0d
			y: 19.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["37CEE1000998A174"]
			description: ["A racetrack is a nanowire along which magnetic domains move like cars on a track. It stores more bits per area than any plain memory. The Cluster Tool lays a synthetic antiferromagnet over the MRAM wafer (circuit 3, 600 ticks). The nitride magnet works anneals it (circuit 10) and electron beam refining writes the track (circuit 16). The Cluster Tool then patterns the nanowires (circuit 1; a quarter of the platinum comes off as sludge) and joins the MTJ die for the racetrack chip (circuit 2, 900 ticks). The oscillator module, which is grown on the racetrack chip. Keep the platinum sludge in a chest or send it to the platinum line; it is the byproduct that pays for the sputter targets."]
			icon: "grindless:racetrack_chip"
			id: "399C5261E9B68BA2"
			rewards: [{ id: "1C2C5CAD23A227CD", type: "xp", xp: 160 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "1E11BB949B48A4F5", item: "grindless:saf_track_wafer", type: "item" }
				{ id: "59D4A8A4758AD0E6", item: "grindless:patterned_track_wafer", type: "item" }
				{ id: "7190BE84051757FC", item: "grindless:racetrack_chip", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Racetrack"
			x: 36.5d
			y: 19.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["794B4368FD9DDBD0"]
			description: ["A spin-torque oscillator turns a direct current into a microwave signal through the spin of its electrons. An array of them drives the spin-wave bus. The Cluster Tool sputters the oscillator stack on the racetrack chip (circuit 4, 700 ticks). Electron beam refining defines the pillars (circuit 27), the ion implanter mills them (circuit 10), a chemical bath with hydrochloric acid cleans the redeposit, and the MOCVD reactor planarises with silane and ammonia (circuit 15). The Photonic Foundry caps the array with gold (circuit 20). The magnonic bus. Acid and silane by pipe; the bath returns its redeposit as dust."]
			icon: "grindless:stno_array"
			id: "76FB3CD0A40C8C78"
			rewards: [{ id: "3501A375BDBB9CB3", type: "xp", xp: 160 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "14414E2ECC92B98C", item: "grindless:stno_stack_wafer", type: "item" }
				{ id: "32AFE95DB963AB52", item: "grindless:stno_array", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Spin-Torque Oscillators"
			x: 29.5d
			y: 22.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["76FB3CD0A40C8C78"]
			description: ["A yttrium iron garnet film carries spin waves with almost no loss, and the oscillator array drives them: together they make the bus that moves data inside the chip. The &6YIG LPE Furnace&r grows the film on a GGG wafer in a platinum crucible (circuit 2, 1,200 ticks), and electron beam refining cuts the waveguides (circuit 17). An assembler (800 ticks) joins the waveguide wafer, the oscillator array, a 5N platinum part, a platinum sheet and soldering alloy. The ME-on-spin wafer. The flux comes back from the skim recipe (circuit 3); keep a spare platinum crucible."]
			icon: "grindless:magnonic_bus"
			id: "5A380D3D56FF29FD"
			rewards: [{ id: "512246B62B456BE7", type: "xp", xp: 180 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "1254C5FBC01B63E5", item: "grindless:yig_film_wafer", type: "item" }
				{ id: "705BDE472474A258", item: "grindless:yig_waveguide_wafer", type: "item" }
				{ id: "11CE0DA11E4B1C62", item: "grindless:magnonic_bus", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Magnonic Bus"
			x: 33.0d
			y: 22.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5A380D3D56FF29FD"]
			description: ["A magnetoelectric membrane flips a magnet with a voltage instead of a current, so it switches with far less heat. It is made of oxides that only grow in a pulsed laser plume. The Cluster Tool, with a KrF laser and oxygen: a strontium ruthenate electrode on a dysprosium scandate substrate (circuit 1, 400 ticks), a bismuth ferrite film (circuit 2) and a cobalt-iron layer (circuit 3). Electron beam refining then patterns the switch (circuit 19). The ME-on-spin wafer. Oxygen by pipe; the bismuth fume is a byproduct and goes to the fume scrubber."]
			icon: "grindless:me_switch_wafer"
			id: "7AC8ABCAA1CCFF90"
			rewards: [{ id: "5E6E7B61E544053E", type: "xp", xp: 160 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [
