		{
			dependencies: ["76FB3CD0A40C8C78"]
			description: ["Spin-orbit torque reads the bit out through a stack of two-dimensional crystals: a heavy metal, a magnet and a barrier a few atoms thick, each laid on the last by the vdW stacker. The vdW stacker in its UXV mode cleaves WTe2 and FGT flakes (circuits 1 and 2), then stacks them with hBN into a heterostack under argon (circuit 4, 900 ticks). Electron beam refining adds gold edge contacts (circuit 18) and the nitride magnet works anneals the stack (circuit 12). The MESO spin wafer, where the readout is laid over the magnetoelectric layer. Crystals by ME; broken flakes come out as dust, send it back to the crystal line."]
			icon: "grindless:sot_readout_stack"
